ering in Agriculture v1.1\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nProject Carcará\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n27 Jul 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 204.95 tCO₂e removed from Project Carcará on 18 Aug 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n204.947 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n273.187 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n66.455 tCO₂e\\n-\\nUncertainty Discount\\n1.784 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nParaguaçu\\tMineral & rock\\t09 Mar 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n17 Mar 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Mar 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Aug 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Aug 2025\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Jul 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 5\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n204.95\\nRetired\\n44.3\\nBuffer pool\\n4.099\\nCrediting period\\n29 Apr 2024 to 29 Apr 2029\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n17 Mar 2026\\t204.95\\t4.099\\t200.851\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Terradot's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 4.099 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 4.099 certificates.\\n\\nTerradot has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"